IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- the dog owner's questions: must I register my dog, and when does the
-- registration end (ss 7, 15, 16); what does registration cost, with the concessions (s 15 and Dog Regulations 2013
-- rr 17-20); what refund do I get if I sterilise it later (r 19); must I microchip it and tell the shire (ss 21-23);
-- may the shire refuse to register it (s 16(3), (3A)); is it lawfully in this public place (ss 30-32); is it a
-- dangerous dog, and what follows from a declaration (ss 3, 33E, 33F); and the most I can be fined for the
-- registration and microchipping offences (ss 7(1), 21, 22, and the modified penalties in r 33).
--
-- SEAT: the dog owner. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Must I register my dog", "How much is
-- the registration fee", "Must my dog be microchipped", "Is my dog lawfully in this public place", "By when must I
-- object to the declaration". Where a provision addresses the local government, it is encoded as what may be done to
-- the owner (refusal, declaration) and by when.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 (dangerous dog, dangerous dog (restricted breed), commercial security dog, attack,
-- provocation, sterilised, townsite), s 7(1), (3)(a)-(c), s 15(1)-(6), s 16(1), (2), (3), (3A), s 21(2), (4), (5),
-- s 22(2)-(6), s 23, s 30(1)-(4), s 31(1), (2), (2A), (3), (4), s 32(1)-(5), s 33E(1), s 33F(2), (3).
--
-- Edition: the compilation with editorial changes as at 26 November 2024 (amendments in force to 28 November 2024, from
-- the Dog Amendment (Stop Puppy Farming) Act 2021), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47983.txt
-- (retrieved 7 September 2026). Regulations: Dog Regulations 2013, version 01-j0-00 (currency start 24 July 2025), as
-- deposited at ../../../dog-regulations-2013/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48740.txt (retrieved 20 October 2026):
-- r 4 (restricted breeds), r 11 (RWWA), r 17 and its Table (fees), r 18 (3-year period), r 19 (refund on later
-- sterilisation), r 20(3) (proof of sterilisation), r 27 (2-metre leash), r 33 Table item 1 (modified penalties).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the uncommenced provisions of the Dog Amendment (Stop Puppy Farming) Act 2021 (the compilation lists
-- them as "To be proclaimed"; s 3 already refers to an "approval to breed" in s 26I, which is not in the deposit);
-- s 7 as it binds an occupier; s 8 (assistance dog access: asked as a fact); s 16A, s 26B-26D (transfer and change
-- notices); s 26 (numbers of dogs, local laws); s 27 (kennels: the r 17 kennel fee is per establishment); s 33
-- (greyhounds); s 33A (private places); s 33D (attacks: offences); s 33GA-33M (what a dangerous dog's owner must do,
-- seizure, destruction, SAT review); s 38 (nuisance); s 46A (court orders: asked as a fact); the s 15(3)(e), (f)
-- concessions (kennels, prescribed circumstances); s 21(1) (the 2013 transitional limb, overtaken by s 21(2) from
-- 1 November 2015); the shire's local laws (asked as facts: exercise areas, rural leashing areas, prohibited places).
-- Machinery out: Part II (administration), ss 13A, 13B, 14, 18, 24, 25, Part VIA (pet shops, dog supply), Part VIII.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dog Act 1976 -- the dog owner's questions`

§§ `The dog, and the facts about it`

-- r 4 prescribes the restricted breeds for the definition of "dangerous dog (restricted breed)" in s 3(1). Paragraph
-- (g) borrows the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956 (Cth): whether a breed is one of those is asked as a fact.
DECLARE Breed IS ONE OF
    `dogo Argentino`
    `fila Brasileiro`
    `Japanese tosa`
    `American pit bull terrier`
    `pit bull terrier`
    `perro de presa Canario or presa Canario`
    `a breed whose importation the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956 prohibit absolutely`
    `any other breed`

-- s 7(3)(b), (c): who is holding the dog. r 11 adds RWWA to the RSPCA WA and the Dogs Refuge Home in s 7(3)(b).
DECLARE Custodian IS ONE OF
    `me, the owner`
    `the RSPCA WA, the Dogs Refuge Home or RWWA, at a place for finding dogs homes`
    `a vet in the course of professional practice`
    `a police officer or other person performing a function under a written law`

DECLARE Dog HAS
    `age in months`                        IS A NUMBER
    `breeds`                               IS A LIST OF Breed     -- one breed, or every breed in a mix (s 3(1) "a mix of 2 or more breeds")
    `declared dangerous`                   IS A BOOLEAN           -- a declaration under s 33E(1) has effect (s 33F(3))
    `kept to guard others' non-dwelling premises` IS A BOOLEAN    -- s 3(1) "commercial security dog": kept primarily to guard premises that are not dwellings and not the owner's
    `sterilised`                           IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 3(1A): "made permanently infertile"
    `sterilisation proved`                 IS A BOOLEAN           -- r 20(3): a vet's certificate or statutory declaration, or the ear tattoo
    `microchipped`                         IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 3(1): implanted with a prescribed microchip in a prescribed manner (rr 6, 10)
    `vet certificate against microchipping` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 21(4), 22(4): a vet certifies a microchip "may adversely affect the health and welfare of the dog"
    `assistance dog`                       IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 8(1): asked as a fact
    `used for droving or tending stock`    IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 15(5): "bona fide used in the droving or tending of stock"
    `already registered`                   IS A BOOLEAN           -- registered under this Act, or the law of another State or a Territory, and in effect
    `held by`                              IS A Custodian

§§ `s 3 -- is my dog a dangerous dog`

-- s 3(1): "dangerous dog means a dog that is -- (a) a dangerous dog (declared); or (b) a dangerous dog (restricted
-- breed); or (c) a commercial security dog". (b): "of a breed prescribed by the regulations to be a restricted breed;
-- or ... a mix of 2 or more breeds, one being a breed prescribed".
GIVEN b IS A Breed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a restricted breed` b IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `any other breed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN dog IS A Dog
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` dog IF
    any (GIVEN b YIELD `is a restricted breed` b) (dog's `breeds`)

@export Is my dog a "dangerous dog" under the Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 3(1)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog IF
        dog's `declared dangerous`
    OR  `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` dog
    OR  dog's `kept to guard others' non-dwelling premises`

§§ `s 7 -- must I register my dog`

-- s 7(1): "if a dog is not registered under this Act or the law of another State or a Territory each of the following
-- persons commits an offence -- (a) the owner of the dog". (3): not "(a) a dog under the age of 3 months"; nor "(b) a
-- dog held in the custody of" the RSPCA WA, the Dogs Refuge Home or a prescribed body (RWWA, r 11) "in a place
-- maintained for the purpose of finding dogs suitable homes"; nor "(c)" a dog held by a vet, a police officer or a
-- person performing a function under a written law. s 16(1): registered by "the local government of the district in
-- which ... the dog is ordinarily kept". An assistance dog is registered too: s 15(4) only waives its fee.
DECLARE `Registration answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: register it with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept (ss 7(1), 16(1))`
    `no: it is already registered under this Act or another State's or Territory's law (s 7(1))`
    `no: it is under 3 months old (s 7(3)(a))`
    `no: not while a shelter, vet or official holds it (s 7(3)(b), (c))`

@export Must I register my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A `Registration answer`
DECIDE `Must I register my dog` dog IS
    BRANCH
        IF dog's `already registered`
            THEN `no: it is already registered under this Act or another State's or Territory's law (s 7(1))`
        IF dog's `age in months` LESS THAN 3
            THEN `no: it is under 3 months old (s 7(3)(a))`
        IF `is held by its owner` dog
            THEN `yes: register it with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept (ss 7(1), 16(1))`
        OTHERWISE `no: not while a shelter, vet or official holds it (s 7(3)(b), (c))`
    WHERE
        `is held by its owner` d MEANS
            CONSIDER d's `held by`
            WHEN `me, the owner` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(1) penalty: "(a) for an offence relating to a dangerous dog, a fine of $10 000; (b) ... other than a dangerous
-- dog, a fine of $5 000". s 7(2): on conviction the court also orders payment of the fee that should have been paid.
@export What is the most I can be fined for keeping my dog unregistered (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1))?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for an unregistered dog` dog IS
    IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

-- r 33(2), (3) and Table item 1: the modified penalty (infringement notice) for s 7(1) is $200, or $400 for a
-- dangerous dog.
@export What is the infringement notice amount for an unregistered dog (Dog Regulations 2013 r 33, item 1)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the infringement amount for an unregistered dog` dog IS
    IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog THEN 400 ELSE 200

§§ `s 16(3), (3A) -- can the shire refuse to register my dog`

-- s 16(3A): if a person is banned under s 46A(2), a registration officer "is not to effect or renew the registration of
-- a dog in the person's name". s 16(3): the local government "may direct the registration officer to refuse" if
-- "(a) the applicant ... has been convicted, or has paid a modified penalty, within the previous 3 years in respect of
-- 2 or more offences against any of this Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002; or (b) the dog ... has
-- been shown to the satisfaction of the local government to be destructive, unduly mischievous, or to be suffering
-- from a contagious or infectious disease; or (c) the local government is not satisfied that the dog is, or will be,
-- effectively confined ...; or (da) the dog is required under section 21 or 22 to be microchipped but is not
-- microchipped; or (d) the dog is a dangerous dog." The local government's satisfaction is asked as a fact.
-- s 16(4): if it refuses, it must "forthwith notify" the owner with written grounds; s 17(1): review by the SAT.
DECLARE `Refusal answer` IS ONE OF
    `it must refuse: I am banned from owning or keeping a dog by an order under s 46A(2) (s 16(3A))`
    `it may refuse, if the local government so directs; it must give me written grounds and I may seek SAT review (ss 16(3), (4), 17(1))`
    `no ground in s 16(3): the registration officer is to register it (s 16(2)(a))`

@export Can the local government refuse to register my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 16(3), (3A))?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `banned by a s 46A(2) order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court order under s 46A(2) bans you from owning or keeping a dog
      `2 or more offences in the last 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the last 3 years, you were convicted of or paid a modified penalty for 2 or more offences under the Dog Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002
      `shown to be destructive, mischievous or diseased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government is satisfied the dog is destructive, unduly mischievous, or has a contagious or infectious disease
      `the shire is satisfied it will be effectively confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government is satisfied the dog is or will be effectively confined at the premises where it is kept
GIVETH A `Refusal answer`
DECIDE `Can the shire refuse to register my dog` dog `banned by a s 46A(2) order` `2 or more offences in the last 3 years` `shown to be destructive, mischievous or diseased` `the shire is satisfied it will be effectively confined` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `banned by a s 46A(2) order`
            THEN `it must refuse: I am banned from owning or keeping a dog by an order under s 46A(2) (s 16(3A))`
        IF     `2 or more offences in the last 3 years`
            OR `shown to be destructive, mischievous or diseased`
            OR (NOT `the shire is satisfied it will be effectively confined`)
            OR `Am I in breach of the microchipping duty` dog FALSE
            OR `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `it may refuse, if the local government so directs; it must give me written grounds and I may seek SAT review (ss 16(3), (4), 17(1))`
        OTHERWISE `no ground in s 16(3): the registration officer is to register it (s 16(2)(a))`

§§ `s 15 and Dog Regulations 2013 rr 17-20 -- how much is the registration fee`

-- s 15(2): a registration (other than a dangerous dog's) runs to "the next 31 October", or for "an extended period
-- prescribed" (3 years, r 18), or "for a dog's lifetime".
DECLARE Term IS ONE OF
    `one year`
    `three years`
    `lifetime`

-- r 17 Table (Dog Regulations 2013, version 01-j0-00). Item 1: "(a) Registration of unsterilised dog other than a
-- dangerous dog for one year (unless owned by pensioner)" $50; "(b) Registration of a dangerous dog for one year" $50.
-- Item 2 (concessional rates, s 15(3), "for dogs other than dangerous dogs"):
--   unsterilised, one year, pensioner             $25
--   sterilised, one year       pensioner $10      otherwise $20
--   sterilised, 3 years        pensioner $21.25   otherwise $42.50
--   unsterilised, 3 years      pensioner $60      otherwise $120
--   sterilised, lifetime       pensioner $50      otherwise $100
--   unsterilised, lifetime     pensioner $125     otherwise $250
-- "pensioner" is "an eligible pensioner as defined in the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992
-- section 3(1)" (r 17(1)): a borrowed term, asked as a fact. "Sterilised" for the fee means sterilisation "proved, in
-- such manner as is prescribed" (s 15(3)(d)): a vet's certificate or a statutory declaration, or the ear tattoo
-- (r 20(3)).
GIVEN `sterilised rate` IS A BOOLEAN, `pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the term` IS A Term
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the r 17 rate` `sterilised rate` `pensioner` `the term` IS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `one year` THEN
        IF `sterilised rate`
            THEN IF `pensioner` THEN 10 ELSE 20
            ELSE IF `pensioner` THEN 25 ELSE 50
    WHEN `three years` THEN
        IF `sterilised rate`
            THEN IF `pensioner` THEN 21.25 ELSE 42.50
            ELSE IF `pensioner` THEN 60 ELSE 120
    WHEN `lifetime` THEN
        IF `sterilised rate`
            THEN IF `pensioner` THEN 50 ELSE 100
            ELSE IF `pensioner` THEN 125 ELSE 250

DECLARE `Fee answer` IS ONE OF
    `the fee in dollars is`
        HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no fee: an assistance dog (s 15(4))`
    `not available: a dangerous dog is registered only to the next 31 October (s 15(3A))`

-- s 15(4B): "Subsections (3) and (4A) do not apply to a dangerous dog": no concession and no local discount, so $50.
-- s 15(4): "No registration fee shall be payable in relation to an assistance dog".
-- s 15(5): a dog "bona fide used in the droving or tending of stock" pays "one quarter of the fee that would otherwise
-- be payable".
-- s 15(6): a dog's FIRST registration "(a) that takes effect after 31 May and before 1 November in the year of the
-- first registration; and (b) that is to have effect until 31 October in that year" pays "one half". Only a one-year
-- registration ends on 31 October of the year it starts, so only that term can be halved.
-- s 15(4A): the local government "may discount or waive a registration fee" -- its discount is asked as a fact.
-- Where more than one reduction applies, the encoding applies them in turn, each to "the fee that would otherwise be
-- payable" (the encoder's reading; the Act does not say how they combine).
@export How much is the registration fee for my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 15; Dog Regulations 2013 r 17)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `I am an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 s 3(1)
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period you choose: one year, three years or the dog's lifetime
      `first registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the dog's first registration
      `date of effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the registration takes effect, ISO 8601
      `local government discount` IS A NUMBER @desc Any discount in dollars the local government gives under s 15(4A); 0 if none
GIVETH A `Fee answer`
DECIDE `How much is the registration fee` dog `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term` `first registration` `date of effect` `local government discount` IS
    BRANCH
        IF dog's `assistance dog`
            THEN `no fee: an assistance dog (s 15(4))`
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog AND (NOT `is one year` `the term`)
            THEN `not available: a dangerous dog is registered only to the next 31 October (s 15(3A))`
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `the fee in dollars is` (`halved if s 15(6)` (`quartered if s 15(5)` 50))
        OTHERWISE `the fee in dollars is` `the reduced fee`
    WHERE
        `is one year` t MEANS
            CONSIDER t
            WHEN `one year` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the reduced fee` MEANS
            max 0 ((`halved if s 15(6)` (`quartered if s 15(5)` `the rate`)) MINUS `local government discount`)
        `the rate` MEANS
            `the r 17 rate` (dog's `sterilised` AND dog's `sterilisation proved`) `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term`
        `quartered if s 15(5)` x MEANS
            IF dog's `used for droving or tending stock` THEN x DIVIDED BY 4 ELSE x
        `halved if s 15(6)` x MEANS
            IF     `first registration`
               AND `is one year` `the term`
               AND DATE_MONTH `date of effect` AT LEAST 6
               AND DATE_MONTH `date of effect` AT MOST 10
            THEN x DIVIDED BY 2
            ELSE x

§§ `s 15(2), (3A) -- when does my dog's registration end`

-- s 15(2): registration of a dog other than a dangerous dog has effect "from the date specified in the registration
-- certificate until -- (a) in the case of registration for an extended period ..., 31 October in the final year of that
-- period ...; or (b) in the case of registration for a dog's lifetime, the dog's death ...; or (c) in all other cases,
-- the next 31 October". (3A): a dangerous dog's registration runs "until the next 31 October".
-- "The final year of that period" is read literally: the calendar year in which the 3-year period from the date of
-- effect ends (the encoder's reading; the Act does not say whether the period is counted from the date of effect or by
-- registration years ending on 31 October).
DECLARE `Registration end` IS ONE OF
    `it ends on`
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `it ends when the dog dies, unless cancelled sooner (s 15(2)(b))`
    `not available: a dangerous dog is registered only to the next 31 October (s 15(3A))`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next 31 October after` d MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH d AT MOST 10
        THEN Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR d)
        ELSE Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1)

@export When does my dog's registration end (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 15(2), (3A))?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period: one year, three years or the dog's lifetime
      `date of effect` IS A DATE @desc The date in the registration certificate from which it has effect, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Registration end`
DECIDE `When does my dog's registration end` dog `the term` `date of effect` IS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `one year` THEN `it ends on` (`the next 31 October after` `date of effect`)
    WHEN `three years` THEN
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `not available: a dangerous dog is registered only to the next 31 October (s 15(3A))`
            ELSE `it ends on` (Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `last day of the 3-year period`))
    WHEN `lifetime` THEN
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `not available: a dangerous dog is registered only to the next 31 October (s 15(3A))`
            ELSE `it ends when the dog dies, unless cancelled sooner (s 15(2)(b))`
    WHERE
        `last day of the 3-year period` MEANS
            Date (Day (Date (DATE_DAY `date of effect`) (DATE_MONTH `date of effect`) (DATE_YEAR `date of effect` PLUS 3)) MINUS 1)

§§ `Dog Regulations 2013 r 19 -- my refund if I sterilise my dog after registering it`

-- r 19(1): one-year registration, dog sterilised "within that period": refund of "the difference between the
-- registration fee paid for that year and the registration fee which would have been payable for a sterilised dog".
-- (2)-(4): 3-year registration, sterilised in the first year: the whole difference; second year: "two-thirds" of it;
-- third year: "one-third". (5): lifetime registration, the same in the 1st, 2nd and 3rd year "after it is registered".
-- A dangerous dog's fee is $50 sterilised or not (s 15(4B), Table item 1(b)), so there is no difference to refund.
@export What refund do I get if I sterilise my dog after registering it (Dog Regulations 2013 r 19)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `I am an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 s 3(1)
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period that was paid for
      `fee paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The registration fee you paid, in dollars
      `year of the term sterilised in` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year of the registration the dog was sterilised: 1, 2, 3 or later
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What refund do I get for sterilising my dog` dog `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term` `fee paid` `year of the term sterilised in` IS
    IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
        THEN 0
        ELSE max 0 (`the share` TIMES (`fee paid` MINUS `the r 17 rate` TRUE `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term`))
    WHERE
        `the share` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the term`
            WHEN `one year` THEN
                IF `year of the term sterilised in` EQUALS 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0
            OTHERWISE
                BRANCH
                    IF `year of the term sterilised in` EQUALS 1 THEN 1
                    IF `year of the term sterilised in` EQUALS 2 THEN 2 DIVIDED BY 3
                    IF `year of the term sterilised in` EQUALS 3 THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 3
                    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `ss 21, 22 -- must my dog be microchipped`

-- s 21(2): "On and after 1 November 2015, the owner of a dog that has reached 3 months of age must ensure that the dog
-- is microchipped." Penalty $5 000. (4): exempt if a vet's certificate says a microchip "may adversely affect the
-- health and welfare of the dog"; (5): no such certificate for a dog under 3 months.
-- s 22(2): "the owner of a dangerous dog that has reached 3 months of age must ensure that the dog is microchipped."
-- Penalty "$10 000, but the minimum penalty is a fine of $500". (3): s 22(2) does not apply to a dangerous dog
-- (declared) during the 7 days after the declaration notice, or while an objection or review is pending and 7 days
-- after; (6): "Nothing in subsection (3) affects the operation of section 21(1) or (2)". Section 21's heading says
-- "dogs other than dangerous dogs", but its words reach "a dog", and s 22(6) assumes they do; the encoding follows the
-- words, so during a s 22(3) period the s 21(2) duty remains.
DECLARE `Microchip answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes (s 21(2))`
    `yes: a dangerous dog (ss 21(2), 22(2))`
    `yes (s 21(2)); s 22(2) is suspended during the s 22(3) period`
    `no: it is under 3 months old (ss 21(2), 22(2))`
    `no: exempt by a vet's certificate (ss 21(4), 22(4))`

@export Must my dog be microchipped (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 21, 22)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `in a s 22(3) period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dog declared dangerous: whether it is within 7 days of the declaration notice, or an objection or review is pending or decided within the last 7 days
GIVETH A `Microchip answer`
DECIDE `Must my dog be microchipped` dog `in a s 22(3) period` IS
    BRANCH
        IF dog's `age in months` LESS THAN 3
            THEN `no: it is under 3 months old (ss 21(2), 22(2))`
        IF dog's `vet certificate against microchipping`
            THEN `no: exempt by a vet's certificate (ss 21(4), 22(4))`
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog AND dog's `declared dangerous` AND `in a s 22(3) period`
            THEN `yes (s 21(2)); s 22(2) is suspended during the s 22(3) period`
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `yes: a dangerous dog (ss 21(2), 22(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes (s 21(2))`

GIVEN dog IS A Dog, `in a s 22(3) period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in breach of the microchipping duty` dog `in a s 22(3) period` IF
        (NOT dog's `microchipped`)
    AND CONSIDER `Must my dog be microchipped` dog `in a s 22(3) period`
        WHEN `no: it is under 3 months old (ss 21(2), 22(2))` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `no: exempt by a vet's certificate (ss 21(4), 22(4))` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The most the court can fine: s 22(2) $10 000 for a dangerous dog outside a s 22(3) period; otherwise s 21(2) $5 000.
-- 0 where there is no breach.
@export What is the most I can be fined for not microchipping my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 21(2), 22(2))?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `in a s 22(3) period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dog declared dangerous: whether it is within a s 22(3) period
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not microchipping` dog `in a s 22(3) period` IS
    IF NOT `Am I in breach of the microchipping duty` dog `in a s 22(3) period`
        THEN 0
        ELSE CONSIDER `Must my dog be microchipped` dog `in a s 22(3) period`
             WHEN `yes: a dangerous dog (ss 21(2), 22(2))` THEN 10000
             OTHERWISE 5000

§§ `s 23 -- by when must I tell the shire the microchip number`

-- s 23(1): "The owner of a microchipped dog must, within 7 days of the microchipping, give notice in writing to the
-- local government ... of -- (a) the name of the microchip database company ...; and (b) the microchip's unique
-- identification number". (2): not "if the information has been, or will be, provided with an application to the
-- local government to register the dog". Penalty $5 000.
DECLARE `Microchip notice` IS ONE OF
    `give the local government written notice by`
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no separate notice: the details go with the registration application (s 23(2))`

@export By when must I tell the local government my dog's microchip details (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `date microchipped` IS A DATE @desc The date the dog was microchipped, ISO 8601
      `details given with a registration application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the microchip company and number have been or will be given with an application to register the dog
GIVETH A `Microchip notice`
DECIDE `By when must I give the microchip details` `date microchipped` `details given with a registration application` IS
    IF `details given with a registration application`
        THEN `no separate notice: the details go with the registration application (s 23(2))`
        ELSE `give the local government written notice by` (Date (Day `date microchipped` PLUS 7))

§§ `ss 30-32 -- is my dog lawfully in this public place`

-- s 31(1): "A dog shall not be in a public place unless it is -- (a) held by a person who is capable of controlling the
-- dog; or (b) securely tethered for a temporary purpose, by means of a chain, cord, leash or harness of sufficient
-- strength and not exceeding the prescribed length" -- 2 metres from the base of the dog's neck (r 27).
-- (2A): "Despite subsection (1), a dog shall not be in a public place" the local government specifies as prohibited.
-- (2): exempt from (1) "(a) in a dog exercise area"; "(b) in a public place that is in an area of the State outside the
-- metropolitan region or outside a townsite, and that is not a rural leashing area"; "(c) in or on a vehicle"; and
-- (d)-(h) shows, obedience trials, working stock dogs, foxhounds, customary sporting purposes.
-- s 32(1): in a dog exercise area or such a rural place, a dog must be held, tethered, or "(e) ... not a greyhound and
-- ... supervised by a competent person who is in reasonable proximity" -- (2) a person liable for its control,
-- capable of controlling it, and "carrying and capable of attaching" a leash not over the prescribed length.
-- (3): the s 31(2) exemptions other than (a) and (b) apply to s 32 too.
-- ss 31(3), 32(4): every person liable for the control of the dog commits an offence, $5 000, unless a s 33B defence
-- (all reasonable precautions and due diligence) is made out. ss 31(4), 32(5): not for a dangerous dog (s 33GA).
-- "Metropolitan region" (Planning and Development Act 2005 s 4) and "townsite" (s 3(1), built on the Land
-- Administration Act 1997 and lodged plans) are asked as facts. The s 31(2)(b) words "outside the metropolitan region
-- or outside a townsite" are encoded as written: either suffices.
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary public place`
    `a dog exercise area`
    `a rural leashing area`
    `a public place where the local government prohibits dogs at this time`
    `in or on a vehicle`

DECLARE Control IS ONE OF
    `held on a leash by a person able to control it`
    `securely tethered by a leash for a temporary purpose`
    `off the leash, supervised close by a competent person carrying a leash`
    `off the leash and unsupervised`

DECLARE `Public place answer` IS ONE OF
    `lawful (s 31(1))`
    `lawful: held, tethered or competently supervised in an exercise area or rural place (s 32(1))`
    `lawful: exempt (s 31(2))`
    `offence under s 31(3): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
    `offence under s 32(4): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
    `not encoded: a dangerous dog is controlled under s 33GA`

@export Is my dog lawfully in this public place (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 31, 32)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `the place` IS A Place @desc What kind of public place it is, as the local government has specified it
      `in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in the metropolitan region (Planning and Development Act 2005 s 4)
      `in a townsite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in a townsite as defined in s 3(1)
      `the control` IS A Control @desc How the dog is being controlled
      `leash length in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the leash used or carried, in metres from the base of the dog's neck
      `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 31(2)(d)-(h) activities applies: a show, an obedience trial or class, working stock, a foxhound pack, retrieving or duck hunting
GIVETH A `Public place answer`
DECIDE `Is my dog lawfully in this public place` dog `the place` `in the metropolitan region` `in a townsite` `the control` `leash length in metres` `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog
            THEN `not encoded: a dangerous dog is controlled under s 33GA`
        IF `is prohibited` `the place`
            THEN `offence under s 31(3): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
        IF `is a vehicle` `the place` OR `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose`
            THEN `lawful: exempt (s 31(2))`
        IF `is a s 32 place`
            THEN IF `held or tethered` OR `competently supervised`
                     THEN `lawful: held, tethered or competently supervised in an exercise area or rural place (s 32(1))`
                     ELSE `offence under s 32(4): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
        IF `held or tethered`
            THEN `lawful (s 31(1))`
        OTHERWISE `offence under s 31(3): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
    WHERE
        `is prohibited` p MEANS
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN `a public place where the local government prohibits dogs at this time` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is a vehicle` p MEANS
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN `in or on a vehicle` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is a s 32 place` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the place`
            WHEN `a dog exercise area` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an ordinary public place` THEN (NOT `in the metropolitan region`) OR (NOT `in a townsite`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `leash short enough` MEANS `leash length in metres` AT MOST 2
        `held or tethered` MEANS
            `leash short enough`
            AND CONSIDER `the control`
                WHEN `held on a leash by a person able to control it` THEN TRUE
                WHEN `securely tethered by a leash for a temporary purpose` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE
        `competently supervised` MEANS
            `leash short enough`
            AND CONSIDER `the control`
                WHEN `off the leash, supervised close by a competent person carrying a leash` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 30(1): "A dog must not be in a public place unless it is wearing a collar to which is securely attached a
-- registration tag". (3): not (d) a dog being exhibited for show purposes, (e) one being trained for or taking part in
-- retrieving, duck hunting or another customary sporting purpose, (f) obedience trials, or (a) a greyhound in a
-- licensed race. (4): "This section does not apply to a dangerous dog." (2): $5 000.
@export Must my dog wear a collar with its registration tag in a public place (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN dog IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `at a show, sporting purpose, obedience trial or race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dog is being exhibited, trained for or taking part in a customary sporting purpose, an obedience trial or class, or a licensed greyhound race (s 30(3))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my dog wear its registration tag in public` dog `at a show, sporting purpose, obedience trial or race` IF
        (NOT `Is my dog a dangerous dog` dog)
    AND (NOT `at a show, sporting purpose, obedience trial or race`)

§§ `ss 33E, 33F -- can my dog be declared dangerous, and by when must I object`

-- s 33E(1): the local government, or a person authorised by it, may declare a dog a dangerous dog (declared) "if, in
-- the opinion of the local government or that person -- (a) the dog has caused injury or damage by an attack on, or
-- chasing, a person, animal or vehicle; or (b) the dog has, repeatedly, shown a tendency -- (i) to attack, or chase,
-- ... even though no injury has been caused ...; or (ii) to threaten to attack; or (c) ... other criteria prescribed"
-- (none are prescribed in the deposited Regulations). s 3(1): "attack ... does not include behaviour which was an
-- immediate response to, and was induced by, provocation". The opinion is the local government's: answered
-- conditionally.
DECLARE Incident IS ONE OF
    `an unprovoked attack that caused injury or damage`
    `a chase that caused injury or damage`
    `an attack that was an immediate response to provocation`
    `repeated attacks, chases or threats to attack, without injury`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Declaration answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
    `no: behaviour induced by provocation is not an attack (s 3(1))`
    `no ground in s 33E(1)`

@export Can my dog be declared a dangerous dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33E)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS AN Incident @desc What the dog did
GIVETH A `Declaration answer`
DECIDE `Can my dog be declared dangerous` `what happened` IS
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `an unprovoked attack that caused injury or damage` THEN `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
    WHEN `a chase that caused injury or damage` THEN `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
    WHEN `repeated attacks, chases or threats to attack, without injury` THEN `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
    WHEN `an attack that was an immediate response to provocation` THEN `no: behaviour induced by provocation is not an attack (s 3(1))`
    OTHERWISE `no ground in s 33E(1)`

-- s 33F(2)(b): the owner has a right "to be exercised within not more than 7 days after the giving of the notice" to
-- object to the local government or apply directly to the SAT. (3): "Whether or not an objection is lodged or
-- application for review is made, the declaration ... has effect 7 days after the giving of a notice".
@export By when must I object to, or seek review of, a dangerous dog declaration (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33F(2))?
GIVEN `date notice given` IS A DATE @desc The date the declaration notice was given to you, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object to the declaration` `date notice given` IS
    Date (Day `date notice given` PLUS 7)

@export When does a dangerous dog declaration take effect, even if I object (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33F(3))?
GIVEN `date notice given` IS A DATE @desc The date the declaration notice was given to you, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does the declaration take effect` `date notice given` IS
    Date (Day `date notice given` PLUS 7)
